aws dynamodb create-table \
    --table-name Main_table \
    --attribute-definitions \
        AttributeName=Category,AttributeType=S \
        AttributeName=Publish,AttributeType=S \
        AttributeName=Author,AttributeType=S \
        AttributeName=PaperId,AttributeType=S \
        AttributeName=Keyword,AttributeType=S \
    --key-schema \
        AttributeName=Category,KeyType=HASH \
        AttributeName=Publish,KeyType=RANGE \
    --global-secondary-indexes '[
        {
        "IndexName": "AuthorIndex",
        "KeySchema": [
            {"AttributeName": "Author","KeyType": "HASH"},
            {"AttributeName": "Publish","KeyType": "RANGE"}
        ],
        "Projection": {"ProjectionType": "KEYS_ONLY"}
        },
        {
        "IndexName": "PaperIdIndex",
        "KeySchema": [
            {"AttributeName": "PaperId","KeyType": "HASH"}
        ],
        "Projection": {"ProjectionType": "KEYS_ONLY"}
        },
        {
        "IndexName": "KeywordIndex",
        "KeySchema": [
            {"AttributeName": "Keyword","KeyType":"HASH"},
            {"AttributeName": "Publish","KeyType":"RANGE"}
        ],
        "Projection": {"ProjectionType": "KEYS_ONLY"}
        }
    ]' \
    --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST \
    --table-class STANDARD



aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Main_table \
  --key-condition-expression "Category = :c AND Publish BETWEEN :a AND :b" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{":c":{"S":"cs.LG"},":a":{"S":"0000"},":b":{"S":"9999"}}' \
  --scan-index-forward false


aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Main_table \
  --index-name AuthorIndex \
  --key-condition-expression "Author = :a AND Publish BETWEEN :x AND :y" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{":a":{"S":"Author1"},":x":{"S":"0000"},":y":{"S":"9999"}}' \
  --scan-index-forward false


aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Main_table \
  --index-name KeywordIndex \
  --key-condition-expression "Keyword = :k AND Publish BETWEEN :x AND :y" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{":k":{"S":"keyword1"},":x":{"S":"0000"},":y":{"S":"9999"}}' \
  --scan-index-forward false


aws dynamodb query \
  --table-name Main_table \
  --index-name PaperIdIndex \
  --key-condition-expression "PaperId = :p" \
  --expression-attribute-values '{":p":{"S":"2301.12345"}}'



My strategy is copying each paper into several attributes, this allows for faster queries but this also means that i have many duplicates that leads to more writes which would cost more. This is because DynamoDB diff to SQL and there is no join at read time?

I also chose to make the projection keys only so that the GSIs don't store too much info which could help save some space but it would require a second request if i were to want to get the details and not just the keys. Might change this depending on how much storage i will use after i have coded it.